note.para:
    Most contemporary clients accept relative URIs as argument to
    Location:,
    but some older clients require an absolute URI
    including the scheme, hostname and absolute path. You can usually use
    $_SERVER['HTTP_HOST'],
    $_SERVER['PHP_SELF']
    and dirname to make an absolute URI from a
    relative one yourself:



<?php
/* Redirect to a different page in the current directory that was requested */
$host  = $_SERVER['HTTP_HOST'];
$uri   = rtrim(dirname($_SERVER['PHP_SELF']), '/\\');
$extra = 'mypage.php';
header("Location: http://$host$uri/$extra");
exit;
?>

